{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "That's Christmas To Me feels like a natural next choice because several of my past selections were explicitly Christmas albums.",
    "Christmas At Downton Abbey also connects with that repeated holiday interest, although I would try my first choice before selecting another."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Stages and Encore: Movie Partners Sing Broadway point toward stage songs, which do not match the holiday listening I would choose right now.",
    "The folk retrospective and titles such as Partners, 25, To Be Loved, and Wallflower give me too little connection to my past choices to make me want to explore them."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The selections seem to treat an interest in a few albums as a broad interest in other vocal collections, when the Christmas theme is what draws me to my strongest matches.",
    "A best-of collection does not appeal to me simply because it gathers familiar songs; I still need a clear connection to what I want to hear."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated Christmas selections, including returning to The Classic Christmas Album, are a stronger reason for my interest than a loose resemblance between albums.",
    "My latest selection was The New Old Fashioned after a long gap, so my older holiday listening should be treated as a useful clue rather than certainty about my current mood. I rarely choose something without a clear reason."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The holiday recommendations capture a recurring interest, but most other choices stretch that interest beyond what would motivate me to listen."
}"}
